  "description": "MEKSUR crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: 2(C1 H6 N1 1+),C20 H16 Cl30 Gd4 O30 2-,2(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Gd1 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd2 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd3 (Gd) has 9 O neighbors; Gd4 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 6 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.803-3.879 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 104.75-108.11°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula (NH3CH3)2[Gd4(OH)4(CCl3COO)10(H2O)6]·2H2O. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 4 OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 6 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula). Article name explicitly identifies I(II).",
